{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789217792,"nonce":"TbXk3Xb7zqL3C1cv1ElxwJ9Hg2c=","message":"Done, 7f66752..d3d6158 (16 commits).\n\nThe LLVM backend now translates every AIR v2 instruction from its own fields: air_emit.rs keeps the CFG, phis, terminators, arithmetic, constants, vectors and register allocation; calls.rs, objects.rs, casts.rs, enums.rs and memory.rs hold the rest, one emitter per variant. air_instr_opcode, translate_opcode and opcode.rs are deleted, the instruction match has no catch-all (a new AirInstr is a compile error here), and serialize.rs is the only AIR-to-opcode converter left. The two symptoms this issue named are gone: FieldGet/FieldSet read obj_ty, SetEnumField reads its construct. init_required_natives and the by-name std_hlp_alloc_obj_caller lookup went with it; New declares hlp_alloc_obj like every other helper. Intrinsic is emitted from the kind AIR classified (PtrCompare inline, shared with Cranelift through NativeIntrinsic::of_kind). Both LLVM entry points allocate registers through one AIR-aware routine.\n\nHow it was verified. The unoptimised AOT IR of all 79 test programs was dumped before and after every move commit and stayed byte-identical (value names included); after the deliberate changes the only structural differences were the intended ones. cargo test -p ash / ash_core / ash_interp pass. On Linux (NUC, release): Haxe unit 1069/1069 cases and sys 1118/1118 assertions under AOT, and the same under the hybrid runtime with the LLVM tier pinned as tier 0 at threshold 1 (a wrapper passing --jit-tier llvm --jit-threshold 1; --mode jit refuses ASH_TIER=llvm), plus interp and Cranelift jit on unit after the interpreter change.\n\nFound on the way and fixed: 3a3ef0a (Rethrow), 5c6fb3a (widened functions only lowered through OSR), 7eec021 (virtual closures over inherited methods crashed the AOT build and the interpreter; new fixture test_virtual_closure_inherited). Filed and open: 0b2bd6d, 346c461 (LLVM half done; reload.rs swaps no body yet), 4aa2b09, 1d57ea5, 228d347, 5ca81fb.","files":null}]}